_id":"tvfy_10640","person_slug":"russell-trood","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ruth Webber","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10662","person_slug":"ruth-webber","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sandy Macdonald","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10402","person_slug":"sandy-macdonald","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Fielding","party":"Family First","person_id":"tvfy_10221","person_slug":"steve-fielding","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Hutchins","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10323","person_slug":"steve-hutchins","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Trish Crossin","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10161","person_slug":"trish-crossin","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ursula Stephens","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10609","person_slug":"ursula-stephens","vote":"no"}],"name":"Prohibition of Human Cloning for Reproduction and the Regulation of Human Embryo Research Amendment Bill 2006 - In Committee - Public health benefit","noes":49,"question":"The majority voted against an [amendment](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?gid=2006-11-07.25.1) introduced by Greens Senator [Kerry Nettle](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Kerry_Nettle&mpc=Senate&house=senate), which means it was rejected. Senator Nettle explains that this amendment adds to the list of things that the [National Health and Medical Research Council](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Health_and_Medical_Research_Council) must consider when making a decision about granting licences to people who wish to do stem cell research. It adds: \"_the capacity of any scientific advances to be delivered through the public health system and or to reduce the global disease burden_.\"(Read Senator Nettle's full explanation of this amendment and the surrounding debate [here](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?id=2006-11-07.20.1) after 1:24 pm. ) Due to the sensitive subject matter of this bill, the parties have agreed to allow it to be a free vote.(Read more about what a free vote is in our [FAQ Section](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/faq.php#rebelandfree). More information about the decision to have a free vote on this bill is available on ABC News [here](http://www.abc.net.au/am/content/2006/s1716062.htm). ) _Background to the bill_ The bill was introduced to amend the _Prohibition of Human Cloning Act 2002_ and _Research Involving Human Embryos Act 2002_. The amendments will permit certain [human embryo research](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embryonic_stem_cell) under licence but retain existing prohibitions on [human reproductive cloning](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_cloning) and other assisted reproductive technology activities.(Read information about the bill, including its explanatory memorandum and bills digest, [here](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?bId=s533). ) For example, it proposes to allow for [therapeutic cloning](http://en.","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-1159","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2006-11-07/4"}
